<title>POLAND: Polish crops ratings down in July 21-31.</title>
<headline>Polish crops ratings down in July 21-31.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's Meteorology and Water Management Institute (IMGW) said crop conditions in the July 21-31 period were worse than in the previous 10 days and corresponding 1996 levels, but held above five-year averages.</p>
<p>Ratings are made three times a month based on the condition and development of crops on a scale of one to five, with five the highest grade.</p>
<p> POLISH CROP RATINGS   JULY 31   JULY 20  1996   5-YR AVG</p>
<p> Wheat (winter)	    3.3	 3.4     3.5	n/a</p>
<p> Wheat (summer)	    3.4	 3.5     3.6	3.2</p>
<p> Barley (spring)	   3.4	 3.4     3.5	3.2</p>
<p> Oats			  3.3	 3.4     3.5	3.2</p>
<p> Sugar beets		 3.7	 3.7     3.8	3.3</p>
<p> Potatoes		    3.2	 3.5     3.7	3.2</p>
<p>--Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
